# Potato Vegetable Soup

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1025764-potato-leek-soup](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1025764-potato-leek-soup) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251117233518/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1025764-potato-leek-soup))

{ rating="5" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 Tbsps [unsalted butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" }
- [ ] 1 large [yellow or white onion]{ ing="yellow-or-white-onion" }, finely chopped (about 2 cups)
- [ ] 2 medium [carrots]{ ing="carrots" }, peeled and finely chopped (optional)
- [ ] 2 [celery stalks]{ ing="celery-stalks" }, finely chopped (optional)
- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
- [ ] 1 [garlic clove]{ ing="garlic-clove" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 5 to 6 cups [low-sodium chicken broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] 2 pounds [Yukon Gold potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" }, peeled and cut into 1/2-inch cubes (about 5 cups)
- [ ] 1 fresh or [dried bay leaf]{ ing="dried-bay-leaf" }
- [ ] 1 cup [heavy cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" }
- [ ] [Chopped chives]{ ing="chopped-chives" }, for garnishing
- [ ] [Crusty bread]{ ing="crusty-bread" }, for serving

## Recipe

1. In a large pot, melt [butter]{ ing="unsalted-butter" } over medium. Add [onion]{ ing="yellow-or-white-onion" } (and optional [carrots]{ ing="carrots" } and celery, if using), season with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }, and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened but not browned, 8 to 10 minutes. Add garlic and stir until fragrant, 1 minute.
1. Add [broth]{ ing="low-sodium-chicken-broth" } (use 6 cups if including carrots and celery, 5 cups otherwise), [potatoes]{ ing="yukon-gold-potatoes" } and [bay leaf]{ ing="dried-bay-leaf" }; season with salt, and bring to a boil over medium-high heat. Cover, adjust heat to medium-low and cook at a gentle simmer until potatoes are completely tender, 15 to 20 minutes. Discard bay leaf.
1. Working in two batches, if necessary, transfer soup to a blender and purée just until smooth. (Resist the urge to overprocess in the blender, which can result in gummy soup.) Return soup to the pot or, for an extra-silky soup, strain through a fine-mesh sieve into the pot.
1. Stir in [cream]{ ing="heavy-cream" } and warm over medium-low heat, stirring frequently, for about 2 minutes. Season with salt.
1. Divide soup among bowls and garnish with [chives]{ ing="chopped-chives" }. Serve warm, with [crusty bread]{ ing="crusty-bread" }.

## Notes

- Loved by kids!
- Yukon Gold potatoes have golden flesh that’s denser and sweeter than other potatoes, giving the soup a richer texture and greater depth of flavor
